-- title:
--   Orbit of Γ₁(ℓ_g)-level structures has at least 2[SL₂(ℤ):±Γ_{H_1}] elements
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number coprime to $q$, and let $\ell_g$ be a prime with $\ell_g \ge 3$ dividing $M'$. Let $H_1$ be the subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ given by the intersection of the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ with the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell_g$. Let $V$ be an additive commutative group and $B_1, B_2 \in V$ elements annihilated by $qM'$ such that $a \cdot B_1 + b \cdot B_2 = 0$ with $a,b \in \mathbb{Z}$ forces $qM' \mid a$ and $qM' \mid b$, and such that every $v \in V$ annihilated by $qM'$ is an integral combination of $B_1$ and $B_2$; thus the $qM'$-torsion of $V$ is free of rank two over $\mathbb{Z}/qM'$ on $B_1, B_2$. Let $P_1, P_2 \in V$ be annihilated by $q$ and independent modulo $q$ (if $a \cdot P_1 + b \cdot P_2 = 0$ then $q \mid a$ and $q \mid b$), let $C \le V$ be an additive subgroup which is cyclic of cardinality $M'$, and let $P \in C$ be a nonzero element annihilated by $\ell_g$. Finally let $G$ be a set of additive automorphisms of $V$ realising on the pair $(B_1,B_2)$ every integral matrix of determinant congruent to $1$ modulo $qM'$: for all integers $a,b,c,d$ with $qM' \mid ad - bc - 1$ there is $g \in G$ with $g B_1 = a \cdot B_1 + c \cdot B_2$ and $g B_2 = b \cdot B_1 + d \cdot B_2$. Then twice the index in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the subgroup generated by $-1$ together with [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) — the group of matrices in $\Gamma_0(q^2M')$ whose lower right entry reduces into $H_1$ — is at most the cardinality of the set of quadruples $(g P_1, g P_2, g(C), g P)$ in $V \times V \times \mathrm{AddSubgroup}(V) \times V$ with $g \in G$.
--
--   This is the orbit-counting half of a comparison between the degree of a modular curve invariant and the number of level structures of type $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ lying in a single $\mathrm{SL}_2$-orbit: the index of $\pm\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ bounds from below the number of distinct quadruples obtained by moving a fixed structure $(P_1,P_2,C,P)$ by the automorphisms in $G$. It feeds the estimate [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.index_le_finrank_adjoin_jOf_of_transcendental_jOf_rigidDataH1Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.index_le_finrank_adjoin_jOf_of_transcendental_jOf_rigidDataH1Pow).
